WEBVTT

00:37.920 --> 00:39.988
All right, who's ready
for a little tailgating?

00:40.022 --> 00:42.324
Hey, Brian,
toss me a cold one!

00:43.459 --> 00:46.127
Ah. Nothing better
than a 7:00 a.m. beer

00:46.162 --> 00:47.629
in an unbrushed mouth.

00:47.663 --> 00:49.598
Peter, I don't want
you drinking too much.

00:49.632 --> 00:50.799
You're driving
us all home.

00:50.833 --> 00:53.001
Lois, I know
how many beers I can drink

00:53.035 --> 00:54.469
and still be able to drive.

00:54.503 --> 00:55.637
I figured it out.

01:04.647 --> 01:06.848
Seven.

01:07.883 --> 01:09.484
Six.

01:12.355 --> 01:15.457
Hey, Cleveland,
what are you doing back in town?

01:15.491 --> 01:17.692
Just back up here
for my monthly haircut.

01:17.727 --> 01:20.829
When a black man finds
a barber, it's for life.

01:20.863 --> 01:23.498
Oh, my God, there's the CEO
of my company!

01:23.532 --> 01:25.100
Now's my chance
to impress him.

01:25.134 --> 01:26.534
Hey, Mr. Carlisle!

01:26.569 --> 01:28.169
Check this out.

01:30.373 --> 01:32.440
That's what I can do
for the company.

01:32.475 --> 01:33.708
Really?

01:33.743 --> 01:35.944
<i>Can you do other
things for the company?</i>

01:35.978 --> 01:38.513
No! No! No! I don't want
to be promoted that way!

01:38.547 --> 01:39.681
I want to be promoted

01:39.715 --> 01:41.549
the shooting-hawks
with-a-crossbow way.

01:42.585 --> 01:44.953
"The NFL experience."

01:44.987 --> 01:46.321
That sounds cool.

01:46.355 --> 01:47.522
Kid, you're the best.

01:47.556 --> 01:49.424
Sign with me, and you're
gonna make millions.

01:49.458 --> 01:50.825
Griffin, get out there!

01:50.860 --> 01:51.993
Ow!
It's his knee.

01:52.028 --> 01:53.161
Doc?!

01:53.195 --> 01:54.475
You'll never
play football again.

01:54.497 --> 01:55.630
Too bad, kid.

01:55.665 --> 01:57.499
You was gonna
buy me a house!

01:57.533 --> 01:59.200
Now I have headaches.

01:59.235 --> 02:01.369
I'm gonna save my brain
for science.

02:02.872 --> 02:04.406
Come on, guys.
It's game time.

02:04.440 --> 02:06.207
Yeah!
Patriots!

02:06.242 --> 02:08.743
All right! This is the greatest
Sunday tradition ever.

02:08.778 --> 02:10.578
Except for getting
all my cutaway gags

02:10.613 --> 02:11.980
ready for the week.

02:12.014 --> 02:15.150
Okay, my Great-Uncle-wears
a-ski-hat-all-the-time Griffin

02:15.184 --> 02:17.152
will be followed
by Nick Nolte's handkerchief,

02:17.186 --> 02:19.521
followed by Japanese Abe
Lincoln, and then monkey rabbi.

02:19.555 --> 02:21.923
Hey, where's the monkey rabbi?

02:21.957 --> 02:24.192
Here's your Torah.
You be here on Tuesday at 9:00.

02:24.226 --> 02:25.193
Check in with Shirley.

02:25.227 --> 02:26.594
You gonna need me
this week?

02:26.629 --> 02:28.029
Ah, maybe.
Maybe, Friday.

02:28.064 --> 02:29.597
Uh, now, where are the gays?

02:29.632 --> 02:31.833
Over here.
No, no, no, the really cartoony gays?

02:31.867 --> 02:33.368
Yoo-hoo!

02:33.402 --> 02:35.570
There you are. We're gonna
need you guys all week.

02:41.243 --> 02:43.144
Okay, Brian, so what are the rules?
What?

02:43.179 --> 02:45.180
Rules? What are the rules?
How do you make points?

02:45.214 --> 02:46.715
Oh, no.
Come on, we're here.

02:46.749 --> 02:48.616
Just give me
the Cliff Notes version.

02:48.651 --> 02:50.685
Like-like who's the guy
with the football ball?

02:50.720 --> 02:52.020
It's just called
a football.

02:52.054 --> 02:55.090
Okay, okay, shorthand lingo.
I like it. I like it.

02:55.124 --> 02:57.058
Now, I see some elements
of Red Rover

02:57.093 --> 02:58.927
with a little bit
of spud mixed in.

02:58.961 --> 03:01.229
And is anyone ever going
to blow a raspberry

03:01.263 --> 03:02.530
on the quarterback's belly?

03:02.565 --> 03:03.765
No, Stewie, that
never happens.

03:03.766 --> 03:05.166
Down goes Brady!

03:05.201 --> 03:07.502
And it looks like
Williams is pulling up his shirt

03:07.536 --> 03:09.371
and having a little fun
with his tummy!

03:09.405 --> 03:11.072
Look! He's doing it!

03:11.107 --> 03:12.907
Aw, this is my favorite part
of the game.

03:12.942 --> 03:15.043
When two drunk guys,
each holding a baby,

03:15.077 --> 03:16.411
get into a fistfight.

03:16.445 --> 03:17.679
You're stupid!

03:17.713 --> 03:19.714
No, you're stupid!

03:19.749 --> 03:21.516
Oh, now their wives
are getting into it.

03:21.550 --> 03:22.751
They're gonna put
their cigarettes

03:22.785 --> 03:24.052
in their mouths
and bump boobs.

03:24.086 --> 03:26.321
You got no class,
you bitch!

03:26.355 --> 03:28.089
<i>No, you got no class!</i>

03:28.124 --> 03:30.792
And now here comes security
to kick out the wrong person.

03:30.826 --> 03:34.396
Come on, Miyagi,
take that karate outside!

03:36.432 --> 03:38.299
With a five-point lead
and only ten seconds left,

03:38.334 --> 03:41.169
all the Patriots have to do
is kneel down with the ball,

03:41.203 --> 03:44.105
and the game is...
Oh, my God, it's a fumble!

03:44.140 --> 03:45.540
It's picked up by the Bills,

03:45.574 --> 03:48.042
and they're gonna score
the game-winning touchdown!

03:49.345 --> 03:50.478
Oh, come on!

03:50.513 --> 03:52.347
My God,
ten losses in a row?!

03:52.381 --> 03:54.382
This whole season's been
one long bad dream.

03:54.417 --> 03:56.785
Yeah, like that one
where I walk into the bank,

03:56.819 --> 03:58.486
and I ain't got
no clothes on.

03:58.521 --> 04:00.688
Sir, what are you doing?
You have no clothes on.

04:00.723 --> 04:03.158
Ah, must be having one
of those dreams again.

04:03.192 --> 04:04.826
Better wake myself up.

04:04.860 --> 04:06.694
Oh, thank God.

04:06.729 --> 04:09.764
Well, time to apply for
this small business loan.

04:13.869 --> 04:16.304
We now return to Turner
Classic Movies' presentation

04:16.338 --> 04:20.375
<i>of John Wayne's final Western,
Big Bill Doyle.</i>

04:23.946 --> 04:26.915
Big Bill, two men got off
the 2:40 from Amarillo.

04:26.949 --> 04:28.850
Saddle my horse.

04:28.884 --> 04:31.786
John Wayne only ate beef
and coffee for every meal,

04:31.821 --> 04:34.155
so the director had to shoot
around the fact

04:34.190 --> 04:36.157
that he was on the toilet
all the time.

04:37.693 --> 04:39.694
Reach for the sky, pilgrims.

04:41.297 --> 04:42.764
Big Bill Doyle!

04:42.798 --> 04:43.965
That's right.

04:43.999 --> 04:46.868
And I just made
a Big Bill coil.

04:46.902 --> 04:48.269
Damn it,
I'm so angry

04:48.304 --> 04:49.671
the stupid
Pats lost.

04:49.705 --> 04:50.939
And to Buffalo!

04:50.973 --> 04:52.474
Buffalo's got
everything.

04:52.508 --> 04:54.175
They don't need
a win like this.

04:54.210 --> 04:56.110
You know, I am gonna
channel this anger

04:56.145 --> 04:57.412
into something useful.

04:57.446 --> 04:59.447
Like trying to get sand
out of my backpack.

05:01.250 --> 05:02.784
(yelling

05:02.818 --> 05:05.487
It's been four years
since I went to the beach!

05:05.521 --> 05:06.855
Try turning it
inside out.

05:06.889 --> 05:08.356
Don't you think
I tried that?!

05:08.390 --> 05:09.891
That's the first
thing I did!

05:09.925 --> 05:12.827
We now return
to the Fox NFL Post-Game Show.

05:12.862 --> 05:14.462
I'm here with
C.J. Spiller.

05:14.497 --> 05:16.831
C.J., you ran for
200 yards today.

05:16.866 --> 05:19.400
How did you manage that
against the Patriots' defense?

05:19.435 --> 05:21.369
Well, we just gelled
as a team today,

05:21.403 --> 05:23.571
and was fortunate
to come away with the win.

05:23.606 --> 05:25.507
All thanks
and praise goes to God.

05:25.541 --> 05:27.408
He really won
this one for us.

05:27.443 --> 05:29.644
Mario Williams, you scored
the winning touchdown.

05:29.678 --> 05:31.679
How does it feel
to beat the Patriots?

05:31.714 --> 05:34.349
I'd like to thank God
and a jury of my peers,

05:34.383 --> 05:37.185
who are both responsible for
me being able to play today.

05:37.219 --> 05:39.254
What the hell?!
This is such bull crap!

05:39.288 --> 05:41.356
Well, what are you talking about?
Isn't it obvious?

05:41.390 --> 05:42.524
God hates the Patriots.

05:42.558 --> 05:43.725
He made 'em lose again!

05:43.759 --> 05:44.893
Peter, uncross your legs.

05:44.927 --> 05:46.794
It's weird to yell
with your legs crossed.

05:46.829 --> 05:49.130
Come on, don't you notice that
whenever the Patriots lose,

05:49.164 --> 05:50.632
the other team
always thanks God?

05:50.666 --> 05:52.634
Huh. Peter does kind of
have a point.

05:52.668 --> 05:54.769
Guys, I'm tired of God
messing with football.

05:54.803 --> 05:56.771
We got to do something
about it!

05:56.805 --> 05:57.939
Like what?

05:57.973 --> 05:59.207
We got to find God

05:59.241 --> 06:00.775
and tell him
to cut the crap.

06:00.809 --> 06:03.011
How many times
is God gonna ruin our Sunday

06:03.045 --> 06:04.879
with both church
and bad football?

06:04.914 --> 06:07.515
It's time someone told God
to stay where He belongs--

06:07.550 --> 06:08.950
in our schools,

06:08.984 --> 06:11.452
and-and telling people where
they can stick their wieners.

06:11.487 --> 06:12.620
Now, what do you say?

06:12.655 --> 06:14.322
Let's go find God!

06:14.356 --> 06:16.024
All right, I'm in!
Me, too!

06:16.058 --> 06:18.026
Let's do this!

06:18.060 --> 06:20.061
Whoa, whoa, Joe, Joe!
What the hell?!

06:20.095 --> 06:21.229
What?

06:21.263 --> 06:23.364
I thought, uh, "Find God"
was a code word.

06:23.399 --> 06:25.500
No. We meant literally
go and find him.

06:25.534 --> 06:28.736
Oh. Well, I already
texted Bonnie.

06:49.283 --> 06:52.919
Ugh. What a night.

06:54.855 --> 06:58.758
Whew! What... a... night.

06:58.792 --> 07:02.795
Ca... ray... zy.

07:03.665 --> 07:05.332
Uh, yes, telegram
for hungover.

07:05.366 --> 07:07.734
Yes, I'll-I'll sign for that,
thank you very much.

07:07.769 --> 07:09.503
Oh, boy.

07:09.537 --> 07:10.971
How was your
night, Stewie?

07:11.005 --> 07:13.006
Ugh! Get your own life, bro.

07:13.041 --> 07:14.675
Get off my sack.

07:14.709 --> 07:17.177
Well, Lois, the guys and
I are off to find God.

07:17.212 --> 07:18.645
Peter, that's ridiculous.

07:18.680 --> 07:20.047
This is ridiculous?

07:20.081 --> 07:22.683
There's 500 old grocery
bags neatly folded

07:22.717 --> 07:24.485
and crammed into
one of our cabinets.

07:24.519 --> 07:26.153
I'm leaving those
for the kids.

07:26.187 --> 07:27.988
Peter, the idea of God,
let alone

07:28.022 --> 07:30.090
that he'd care anything
about football, is absurd.

07:30.124 --> 07:33.126
Well, it's absurd to think that
my hand scratching on the couch

07:33.161 --> 07:35.162
is some kind of animal,
but you do.

07:46.741 --> 07:48.509
What the  is that?

07:51.746 --> 07:54.281
Okay, this is God's house,
so we'll just go in there,

07:54.315 --> 07:56.583
talk to Him, and take care
of this whole thing.

07:56.618 --> 07:58.619
It'll be easy as one, two...

08:21.576 --> 08:24.311
Three.

08:24.345 --> 08:25.779
Hang on, guys.

08:25.813 --> 08:28.181
<i>I want to enter the church
like Sherman Hemsley in Amen.</i>

08:28.216 --> 08:30.050
<i>♪ Shine on me
♪ Shine on me ♪</i>

08:30.084 --> 08:31.752
<i>♪ Shine on me
♪ Shine on me ♪</i>

08:31.786 --> 08:34.087
<i>♪ Oh, oh, shine
♪ Shine on me ♪</i>

08:34.122 --> 08:37.658
<i>♪ Oh...
♪ Shine on me ♪</i>

08:37.692 --> 08:39.726
<i>♪ Oh-ah-ah-ah
♪ Shine on me ♪</i>

08:39.761 --> 08:41.762
♪ Hey-hey-hey,
hey-hey-hey, hey-hey-hey... ♪

08:41.796 --> 08:43.530
<i>♪ Shine on me ♪</i>

08:43.565 --> 08:46.066
<i>♪ Oh, oh, oh...
♪ Shine on me... ♪</i>

08:46.100 --> 08:50.237
There was a baby's funeral
going on in there.

08:55.209 --> 08:56.843
Huh. God's all over
this Bible,

08:56.878 --> 08:58.779
but they never give you
an exact address.

08:58.813 --> 09:00.013
You guys, look.

09:00.048 --> 09:01.882
I saw this article
in the paper today.

09:01.916 --> 09:04.184
"First Headline Read Aloud
Often Incorrect."

09:04.218 --> 09:05.953
No, no, not that one,
the one below it.

09:05.987 --> 09:08.488
Oh. "Carrie Underwood
Credits Her Success

09:08.523 --> 09:10.591
to Personal Relationship
With God."

09:10.625 --> 09:12.693
<i>You think she knows
where we can find Him?</i>

09:12.727 --> 09:14.094
I'm sure she does.

09:14.128 --> 09:16.863
She's smart.
She won her job in a contest.

09:16.898 --> 09:19.166
Guys, we are going to Nashville.

09:27.942 --> 09:30.344
Wow, the Country
Music Awards!

09:30.378 --> 09:33.180
And you know it's huge 'cause
it's on a Tuesday night.

09:33.214 --> 09:34.748
Hey, look, there's
Taylor Swift.

09:34.782 --> 09:37.684
And there's Taylor
Not-So-Swift.

09:37.719 --> 09:41.521
♪ I broke up with
a birthday cake. ♪

09:41.556 --> 09:44.257
Ugh. We went on,
like, two dates.

09:45.426 --> 09:47.227
Hey, you're Carrie Underwood,
right?

09:47.261 --> 09:49.363
I sure am.
You want an autograph?

09:49.397 --> 09:51.298
Yeah, can you get me
Randy Travis's?

09:51.332 --> 09:53.367
Uh, I don't think so.

09:53.401 --> 09:55.435
Hey, in that song,
"Jesus, Take the Wheel,"

09:55.470 --> 09:59.039
was that, like, the real Jesus,
or was it just some Mexican guy?

09:59.073 --> 10:01.041
No, it was the
real Jesus.

10:01.075 --> 10:02.309
Wow. So, you know Him?

10:02.343 --> 10:03.877
We're actually looking
for His father.

10:03.911 --> 10:05.579
Do you know
where we can find God?

10:05.613 --> 10:07.514
Well, God is
everywhere.

10:07.548 --> 10:10.517
He's in our hearts, and we take
Him with us wherever we go.

10:10.551 --> 10:12.152
Yeah, we're looking for,
like, an address.

10:12.186 --> 10:14.254
Look, you guys,
I don't know who you are,

10:14.288 --> 10:15.589
but I have
to go perform.

10:15.623 --> 10:17.691
Peter, I don't think
she knows where God is.

10:17.725 --> 10:19.092
Let's go.

10:20.395 --> 10:23.330
Hey, you know I don't like
you talking to other guys.

10:23.364 --> 10:24.931
I'm sorry, Jesus.
Whatever.

10:24.966 --> 10:27.801
Give me 40 bucks.
I want to get a Toby Keith hat.

10:27.835 --> 10:29.803
You sure you don't want
to stay for the show?

10:29.837 --> 10:31.338
Nah. This place
gives me the creeps.

10:31.372 --> 10:33.073
Like when I went to
that Pedophile Opera.

10:33.107 --> 10:36.376
<i>We are proud to
present Mozart's The Magic Flute...</i>

10:36.411 --> 10:38.412
in A minor.

10:40.014 --> 10:42.616
And you still won't give us
an Emmy? Come on!

10:42.650 --> 10:44.217
<i>If Modern Family did that joke,</i>

10:44.252 --> 10:46.486
you'd be carrying 'em around
on your shoulders!

10:50.692 --> 10:52.993
Well, God wasn't in
Nashville either.

10:53.027 --> 10:55.328
Maybe it's time to
throw in the towel.

10:55.363 --> 10:57.397
All right, look, maybe I'm
not like other football fans,

10:57.432 --> 11:00.233
but I don't have a fulfilling
career and a rich family life.

11:00.268 --> 11:02.402
Football is all I got.
Peter's right.

11:02.437 --> 11:04.805
We all live and die
with the Patriots.

11:04.839 --> 11:06.206
Yeah, we got to do this.

11:06.240 --> 11:08.542
Even if it means travelling
to the ends of the Earth.

11:08.576 --> 11:10.544
That's the spirit, guys.
We'll find him.

11:10.578 --> 11:13.113
It can't be any harder
than finding that cheese.

11:13.147 --> 11:14.781
I think the cheese
is that way.

11:14.816 --> 11:16.383
I'm pretty sure
it's over here.

11:16.417 --> 11:19.653
Guys, guys, finding the cheese
is what they want us to do.

11:19.687 --> 11:21.988
Let's just chill.

11:22.023 --> 11:24.391
I don't know where they're
getting all this weed.

11:31.432 --> 11:34.334
"In Greece, it was commonly held
that one could speak to the gods

11:34.368 --> 11:36.069
from the top
of Mount Olympus."

11:36.104 --> 11:37.571
We should probably
go there.

11:37.605 --> 11:39.573
What do you mean "gods"?
There's more than one?

11:39.607 --> 11:41.541
Yes, Peter.
Greece is polytheistic.

11:41.576 --> 11:43.210
<i>Quick, Peter, say something
so he thinks you know</i>

11:43.244 --> 11:44.811
<i>what he's talking about.</i>

11:44.846 --> 11:46.146
Words.

11:46.180 --> 11:47.814
Yeah, you get it.

11:52.787 --> 11:55.288
Apparently, the Greeks have
a bunch of different gods.

11:55.323 --> 11:56.823
Athena's the goddess
of wisdom.

11:56.858 --> 11:58.692
Poseidon is the god
of the sea.

11:58.726 --> 12:00.894
And I am Chronos,
the god of time.

12:00.928 --> 12:02.362
Oh, cool,
what do you do?

12:02.396 --> 12:04.698
I tell the time and
make gift baskets.

12:04.732 --> 12:07.100
So are you also
the god of gift baskets?

12:07.135 --> 12:09.603
I don't know;
you tell me.

12:10.605 --> 12:12.806
Rosewood-mango candle?!

12:12.840 --> 12:14.074
Chronos!

12:14.108 --> 12:15.876
I know, I know.

12:15.910 --> 12:17.911
It's 4:30,
by the way.

12:22.283 --> 12:24.851
All right, what better place
to find God than the birthplace

12:24.886 --> 12:27.454
of all of Western
civilization's great religions

12:27.488 --> 12:28.989
and one really mean one.

12:29.023 --> 12:31.391
I had a feeling this is
what this place would be like.

12:31.425 --> 12:33.660
Oh, God, it's so hot out.
Why is there never any parking downtown?

12:33.694 --> 12:35.996
Who gets married on a Tuesday?
I got to get off these bad feet.

12:36.030 --> 12:37.230
Ailments!

12:37.265 --> 12:39.266
Oh, look, Joe's
feeding 'em pennies.

12:41.803 --> 12:45.038
Oh, oh!
Somebody take a picture.

12:45.072 --> 12:47.774
I can't believe we didn't
find God in Jerusalem.

12:47.809 --> 12:49.276
Well, we'll have
to keep looking.

12:49.310 --> 12:50.777
Oh, here's our bus
to the airport.

12:54.348 --> 12:55.982
Wow.

12:56.017 --> 12:58.819
That was super loud.

13:02.590 --> 13:06.259
Ah, India, the most spiritual
country in the world.

13:13.668 --> 13:16.570
God is not here.

13:20.041 --> 13:21.942
Well, that whole
trip was pointless.

13:21.976 --> 13:24.344
Yeah, plus I left
my Jacuzzi on the whole time,

13:24.378 --> 13:26.246
came home
to a boiled raccoon.

13:26.280 --> 13:27.914
You guys, I feel terrible.

13:27.949 --> 13:30.650
I'm sorry I dragged you around
the world looking for God.

13:30.685 --> 13:32.853
I guess it was
a huge waste of time.

13:32.887 --> 13:35.188
Like bringin' a married guy
to Vegas.

13:35.223 --> 13:36.648
So I'm thinking steak house.

13:36.673 --> 13:38.725
Do they have salad?
I can't eat red meat.

13:38.726 --> 13:42.429
Yeah. Then we hit the tables.
I'm already down 30 bucks.

13:42.463 --> 13:44.598
Maybe the sportsbook.
Is that near Caesars?

13:44.632 --> 13:46.800
I got to get Brandy
a Celine Dion T-shirt.

13:46.834 --> 13:50.136
And then the strip club.
Guys, we have a 7:00 a.m. tee time.

13:50.171 --> 13:52.505
And are we just gonna bail
on the Hoover Dam?

13:52.540 --> 13:54.040
Hey, guys.

13:54.075 --> 13:56.042
Hey, Death.
What are you doing here?

13:56.077 --> 13:58.111
Actually, I'm here
for your show.

13:58.145 --> 14:00.513
Oh, come on, man.
I'm on vacation.

14:00.548 --> 14:02.382
Wait a minute, Death,
you work with God!

14:02.416 --> 14:03.783
Will you take us to Him?

14:03.818 --> 14:05.051
Sure, I guess
I could.

14:05.086 --> 14:07.988
But don't
you mean "her"?

14:08.022 --> 14:10.156
Look at your faces!

14:10.191 --> 14:12.392
Of course it's a dude.
Come on, let's go.

14:17.960 --> 14:20.662
Aw, Death, we really appreciate
you taking us to see God.

14:20.696 --> 14:21.896
No problem.

14:21.931 --> 14:23.331
I was supposed
to kill Russell Brand,

14:23.365 --> 14:25.199
but I'll just
do this instead.

14:25.234 --> 14:26.801
Oh, w-well, wait, wait now.

14:26.835 --> 14:28.903
I mean, you could just
pick us up after...

14:33.642 --> 14:35.610
What the...
Where the hell are we?

14:35.644 --> 14:37.612
This is Heaven.
This is Heaven?

14:37.646 --> 14:39.280
It looks
like a Sandals.

14:39.315 --> 14:41.649
Oh, hey, I'm God.
Welcome to Heaven.

14:41.684 --> 14:43.651
Oh, you got
to be kidding me!

14:43.686 --> 14:45.653
Handicapped is still
a thing up here?

14:45.688 --> 14:47.288
Oh, yeah, you're
like this forever.

14:47.323 --> 14:49.403
Hey, how come everyone
has different kinds of towels?

14:49.425 --> 14:51.726
Well, we don't provide towels;
you have to bring your own.

14:51.760 --> 14:53.861
It's very important
that you die holding towels.

14:53.896 --> 14:55.597
Have the priests
not been passing this along?

14:55.631 --> 14:57.065
It's very important.

14:57.099 --> 14:59.133
You know, I actually can't
believe they let me into Heaven.

14:59.168 --> 15:02.270
They won't even let me umpire
little league games anymore.

15:02.304 --> 15:04.339
Strike two!

15:04.373 --> 15:07.008
And, Ricky, you have got
the best ass on this field.

15:07.042 --> 15:09.811
Look, God, the reason we're
here is we wanted to tell you

15:09.845 --> 15:11.679
to stop messing
with the Patriots!

15:11.714 --> 15:13.147
What?!

15:13.182 --> 15:15.316
You really think I'd get
involved with football games

15:15.351 --> 15:17.452
when there's people dying
in Africa?

15:17.486 --> 15:20.421
Are you gonna do something about
the people dying in Africa?

15:20.456 --> 15:22.090
No, but I'm pretty upset
about it.

15:22.124 --> 15:23.958
Come off it, God,
you know what you're doing.

15:23.993 --> 15:25.560
Stop making
the Patriots lose!

15:25.594 --> 15:27.428
I'm God. I don't
have to do anything.

15:27.463 --> 15:29.097
Ah, so you admit it!

15:29.131 --> 15:30.298
Maybe.

15:30.332 --> 15:31.799
Oh, my God,
it's true?!

15:31.834 --> 15:33.334
You don't, like, pay attention

15:33.369 --> 15:36.404
to how much each individual tips
at each meal, right?

15:36.438 --> 15:39.841
Look, look, God, why... why
you got to hurt Patriots fans?

15:39.875 --> 15:41.542
These are good, drunk people

15:41.577 --> 15:44.245
who work hard to get
absolutely nowhere in life.

15:44.279 --> 15:45.680
There are three million
fishermen

15:45.714 --> 15:47.882
and only seven fish left
in the sea.

15:47.916 --> 15:49.951
But they live to watch football,

15:49.985 --> 15:53.254
many of them still on Zenith
or Sylvania television sets.

15:53.288 --> 15:55.790
Please, God, we're beggin' ya,

15:55.824 --> 15:57.358
leave football alone.

15:57.393 --> 15:58.793
It's all we got.

16:00.162 --> 16:01.663
Look, it-it's not the fans.

16:01.697 --> 16:03.531
It's just...
It's Belichick.

16:03.565 --> 16:04.966
I don't like him.

16:05.000 --> 16:08.536
I gave that guy three Super
Bowls, and he never smiled once.

16:08.570 --> 16:10.705
Not even at home.
Be grateful!

16:10.739 --> 16:12.507
But... but that's
just Belichick.

16:12.541 --> 16:13.708
Yeah, come on, God.

16:13.742 --> 16:16.210
Um, I'm locked out
of my room again.

16:16.245 --> 16:17.945
Oh, yeah, go directly
to the boss.

16:17.980 --> 16:19.681
Don't even try to ask
an employee.

16:19.715 --> 16:21.716
You got to lock
the doors in Heaven?

16:21.750 --> 16:24.652
One guy lost a laptop,
and everybody went nuts.

16:24.687 --> 16:26.587
All right, all right,
I'll tell you what.

16:26.622 --> 16:29.490
If you make Belichick smile,
I'll let the Patriots win again.

16:29.525 --> 16:30.792
Okay, you're on.

16:30.826 --> 16:32.827
I don't know, Peter,
that's gonna be tough.

16:32.861 --> 16:35.396
Don't worry, I got a lot of
practice making people smile.

16:35.431 --> 16:37.899
I used to be a celebrity
baby photographer.

16:37.933 --> 16:40.468
Okay, Apple, Apple,
smile for Peter.

16:40.502 --> 16:42.403
Smile for... No? No?

16:42.438 --> 16:44.405
Okay, okay, look over there.
Who's that? Who's that?

16:44.440 --> 16:46.708
Who loves you over there?
That's right.

16:46.742 --> 16:48.543
Can you smile
for Nanny Number Two?

16:48.577 --> 16:50.411
That's it!
There you go.

16:50.446 --> 16:53.715
And your mommy said that
she'll be able to Skype at 8:30

16:53.749 --> 16:55.917
if drinks don't turn
into dinner.

17:04.593 --> 17:07.061
Okay, okay,
shh, here he comes.

17:07.096 --> 17:08.996
Hiya, Mr. Belichick!

17:09.031 --> 17:11.065
Who the hell are you?
What do you want?

17:11.100 --> 17:12.867
We are here
to make you smile.

17:12.901 --> 17:15.436
And if there's one thing
that always gets me to smile,

17:15.471 --> 17:16.871
it's a child's laughter.

17:16.905 --> 17:18.740
So, I found this kid
in the parking lot,

17:18.774 --> 17:20.575
and I'm gonna make
him laugh for you.

17:24.346 --> 17:25.947
Come on, laugh.

17:25.981 --> 17:27.949
Who's your bubba?
Wudgie, wudgie, wudgie, wudgie.

17:27.983 --> 17:29.650
Don't touch my son's face.

17:29.685 --> 17:31.085
Get over here,
little man.

17:31.120 --> 17:33.154
This flight is cleared
for liftoff.

17:33.188 --> 17:34.522
Vroom. Liftoff.

17:34.556 --> 17:35.723
Whee.

17:35.758 --> 17:36.991
Who's flying?
Whee.

17:37.025 --> 17:38.326
You're flying.
Again.

17:38.360 --> 17:39.560
Who's daddy's
little jet?

17:39.595 --> 17:42.396
I love you,
Daddy.

17:47.302 --> 17:48.970
Oh, God,
you guys again?

17:49.004 --> 17:51.072
All right, Coach,
another surefire equation

17:51.106 --> 17:53.608
for comedy is tragedy plus time.

17:55.477 --> 17:57.578
And now we wait.

17:59.548 --> 18:01.849
All right, Coach, now one
thing that's always funny is

18:01.884 --> 18:04.285
when I dub my voice
over animal footage

18:04.319 --> 18:07.922
and introduce human foibles
into their situations.

18:07.956 --> 18:09.290
Tough day at the bank?

18:09.324 --> 18:10.825
No. Just had a bad lunch.

18:10.859 --> 18:12.393
What did you have?

18:12.427 --> 18:14.595
Serengeti and meatballs.

18:14.630 --> 18:16.998
How absurd!

18:17.032 --> 18:19.600
Look, you guys have been
following me around all day

18:19.635 --> 18:21.035
making fools out
of yourselves.

18:21.069 --> 18:22.503
Would you just
leave me alone?

18:22.538 --> 18:24.071
I've got work to do.

18:24.106 --> 18:26.240
Oh, guys,
I guess we failed.

18:26.275 --> 18:28.075
Sorry for wasting
your time, Coach.

18:28.110 --> 18:29.844
We got to get to
the hospital anyway.

18:29.878 --> 18:31.412
Our friend
Joe here has

18:31.446 --> 18:33.314
to have his fluids
changed every 72 hours,

18:33.348 --> 18:36.284
or else he swells up and
his eyes turn yellow.

18:36.318 --> 18:37.552
Huh.
What was that?

18:37.586 --> 18:38.853
Oh, my God, Joe, quick!

18:38.887 --> 18:40.955
Tell him more
about your sad life.

18:40.989 --> 18:43.991
Uh, every morning, I wake up
drenched in my own urine.

18:44.026 --> 18:47.295
My feet are just shoes sewn
to the bottom of my pants.

18:47.329 --> 18:49.897
Last week, the handicapped seat
on the bus was taken,

18:49.932 --> 18:52.200
so they put me on the front,
like a bicycle.

18:52.234 --> 18:53.868
After I injured my legs,

18:53.902 --> 18:56.871
my doctor said I'd be walking
again in two weeks.

18:56.905 --> 19:00.575
Huh. That's hysterical.

19:00.609 --> 19:01.809
Oh, my God, yes!

19:01.844 --> 19:03.344
All right! All right!
He smiled!

19:03.378 --> 19:04.545
We did it!

19:04.580 --> 19:06.447
Aw, man, this is
my biggest accomplishment

19:06.481 --> 19:09.917
since my 1920s solo flight
across the Atlantic.

19:15.490 --> 19:16.824
<i>Vive Pierre Griffin!</i>

19:16.859 --> 19:17.892
<i>Incroyable!</i>

19:17.926 --> 19:19.060
Don't look in there.

19:19.094 --> 19:20.795
Don't look in there.
It's all craps.

19:20.829 --> 19:22.797
All right, we got to put toilets
in these things

19:22.831 --> 19:25.099
if we're gonna be in 'em
for more than two hours.

19:28.136 --> 19:30.271
Wow. You guys
pulled it off.

19:30.305 --> 19:31.539
Well, a deal's a deal.

19:31.573 --> 19:33.541
I'll leave the
Patriots alone.

19:33.575 --> 19:34.542
Oh, thanks, God!

19:34.576 --> 19:36.611
Yeah!
Really appreciate it.

19:36.645 --> 19:38.212
Aw, come here, you!

19:38.214 --> 19:39.747
Ah, ah, ah!
Get off me!

19:39.781 --> 19:41.382
Get off me!
What the hell?

19:41.416 --> 19:43.651
God's mildly
autistic.

19:43.685 --> 19:45.853
You can't touch Him,
especially on the head.

19:45.888 --> 19:47.729
It's all right, it's all right,
it's all right.

19:47.756 --> 19:49.357
Just-Just-Just
don't do that!

19:49.391 --> 19:50.691
Sorry about that.

19:50.726 --> 19:51.792
Well, uh, again, thanks.

19:51.827 --> 19:52.894
We won't forget this.

19:52.928 --> 19:54.662
Oh, by the way...

19:54.696 --> 19:56.764
Conway Twitty
says cut it out.

19:56.798 --> 19:59.033
Just write a joke.

20:04.072 --> 20:05.406
Well, Peter,
I'm glad you're home,

20:05.440 --> 20:07.808
and I'm happy you guys found
what you were looking for.

20:07.843 --> 20:11.045
Yeah, and this trip made me
realize that 98% of the world

20:11.079 --> 20:12.980
is just making
each other blankets.

20:13.015 --> 20:14.582
So, Brian, you still
an atheist

20:14.616 --> 20:15.816
now that Dad's
met God?

20:15.851 --> 20:17.285
Stewie, who knows
who he met?

20:17.319 --> 20:18.986
Every time we go
to Disney World,

20:19.021 --> 20:21.455
he thinks Mickey Mouse just
happened to be there that day.

20:21.490 --> 20:23.824
I'll tell ya, seeing God in
Heaven was just like that time

20:23.859 --> 20:25.826
I met Mickey and Donald
outside Thunder Mountain.

20:25.861 --> 20:27.061
I mean, what are the odds?

20:27.095 --> 20:28.696
But, Peter, I still
don't understand why

20:28.730 --> 20:30.498
you would go
to all that trouble

20:30.532 --> 20:32.664
to find God and only ask
about the Patriots.

20:32.665 --> 20:33.965
Oh, I asked
for one more thing.

20:35.118 --> 20:37.315
Ah! What's happening?!

20:37.316 --> 20:38.283
Don't look at her.
Don't look at her.

20:38.317 --> 20:39.357
It's okay.
Just go with it.

20:39.385 --> 20:40.559
It'll all be over
in a second.

20:40.560 --> 21:41.560
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru